# HOPEFX-AI-TRADING — Docker build context exclusions
# =============================================================================
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` — anything NOT excluded here gets baked into
# every image layer permanently (readable forever via `docker history`/`docker
# save`/registry push, even after the file is later deleted or rotated on the
# host). This file did not exist before, so `.env` — the runtime secrets file
# generated by deployments/vps_bootstrap.sh / vps_reset.sh — was being copied
# straight into the image. It is injected at runtime via `env_file: .env` in
# docker-compose.yml, so it must never be part of the build context.
# =============================================================================

# ── Secrets — never bake into an image layer ─────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
credentials/
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
admin_password.txt
superadmin_credentials.txt
# NOTE: prop_firm_mode.json (unlike .env) IS committed to git — it ships with
# placeholders only (see CLAUDE.md) and live compliance code
# (risk/compliance/prop_enforcer.py, api/prop_firm.py, ...) reads it at
# runtime, so it must stay in the build context. Only WORDMAP.json (gitignored,
# may hold a real local override) is excluded here — the app falls back to
# WORDMAP.json.example when the real file is absent.
WORDMAP.json
!WORDMAP.json.example
config/risk_appetite.json

# ── VCS / CI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.github/

# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
test-results.xml
*.egg-info/
venv/
.venv/

# ── Node / frontend build tooling (the multi-stage build handles frontend/ itself) ──
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/coverage/
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/
dashboard/node_modules/

# ── Runtime state / data caches (regenerated at runtime, not build inputs) ───
# NOTE: do NOT exclude data/*.csv broadly — api/trading.py, ml/explainability.py,
# ml/ab_baseline.py, backtesting/, and run.py read the intentionally-committed
# data/XAUUSD_50Y.csv / data/XAUUSD_40Y.csv at RUNTIME (not just offline
# training). Only exclude the runtime-generated cache subdirectories, which are
# never source inputs.
logs/
*.log
data/lineage/
data/dukascopy_cache/
data/fred_cache/
data/audit/
state/
kill_switch.flag
mlruns/
mlflow.db
*.rdb

# ── Misc ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: do NOT exclude docs/ or *.md — api/pages.py serves docs/FAQ.md,
# docs/API.md, and docs/MOBILE_GUIDE.md live via real GET routes.
diagnostics/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
